19
00:00:41,916 --> 00:00:44,419
and gathered on his side so it doesn't eat him.

20
00:00:45,086 --> 00:00:46,921
The buffaloes defended them a lot in those days,

21
00:00:46,921 --> 00:00:47,922
और मैस अक्सर
और भैंस अक्सर

22
00:00:48,923 --> 00:00:51,342
Where there is a danger to Gujjars

23
00:00:51,342 --> 00:00:52,719
or a man fell from a tree,

24
00:00:53,094 --> 00:00:54,304
so the buffalo used to come and save them...

25
00:00:54,304 --> 00:00:55,346
Meaning, they helped them [Gujjars].

26
00:00:55,805 --> 00:00:56,431
And the buffalo understood

27
00:00:56,431 --> 00:00:57,974
I mean, there was a relation between Gujjars and buffalo.

28
00:00:58,600 --> 00:00:59,350
One understood the other.

29
00:01:00,435 --> 00:01:01,853
When he realised that the buffalo had gathered around,

30
00:01:01,853 --> 00:01:02,604
he got up...

31
00:01:03,104 --> 00:01:04,063
There was a tiger nearby, speaking...

32
00:01:04,814 --> 00:01:07,275
Then he...shouted and chased away the tiger.
